        "math_academy_id": "q-174431",
        "problem": "Find ${\u22c3}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}$, given that $I={3,5,7},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{3}={-3,0,3},\\,{X}_{5}={3,5},\\,{X}_{7}={-7,0,3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{\u22c3}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one\u00a0}{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u22c3}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i} & ={X}_{3}\\cup {X}_{5}\\cup {X}_{7} \\\\  & ={-3,0,3}\\,\\cup \\,{3,5}\\,\\cup \\,{-7,0,3} \\\\  & ={-7,-3,0,3,5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
